{# DRAFT 6 — one holistic reaction judgment
   Intent: avoid both an exhaustive reason list and a random interruption gate.
   The model makes one broad comparison; Jinja changes only how reluctant it
   should be to displace the current exchange.

   PLACEHOLDERS: followerInterruption and nonFollowerInterruption are proposed
   integer settings. Replace these field names with the actual decorators.
#}
[ system ]
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set zerochance = ss.silenceChancePercent %}
{% set followerInterruption = default(ss.followerInterruption, 3) %}
{% set nonFollowerInterruption = default(ss.nonFollowerInterruption, 2) %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

{% set hasExchange = existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{% set playerSpoke = hasExchange and lastSpeaker.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set playerWasAddressed = hasExchange and lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set silenceAllowed = playerWasAddressed or random < zerochance %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = false %}
{% if playerSpoke and not is_follower(lastDialogueTarget.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% elif playerWasAddressed and not is_follower(lastSpeaker.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% endif %}

# Task

An NPC has completed a line to a recipient. Choose the most natural immediate continuation: one NPC reaction{% if silenceAllowed %}, or `0` if nobody should speak{% endif %}.

Output only {% if silenceAllowed %}`0` or {% endif %}`[exact speaker name]>[exact target]`.

# One selection standard

Consider the completed line, recent dialogue, each candidate's short profile, role, and Interjection guidance together. Choose the candidate whose reaction most specifically belongs immediately after this line.

The information supplied for a candidate is evidence, not a keyword checklist. A candidate may have a valid reaction that is not written verbatim in Interjection guidance, but the reaction must be supported by the supplied context.

The recipient is the natural next speaker because they were addressed. Another candidate may still be more appropriate when their immediate reaction genuinely belongs before the recipient's response.

Do not select someone merely because they are nearby, because a generic line could be written for them, or because silence feels uncomfortable.

Never select {{ lastSpeaker.name }}. That person just spoke.

{% if playerNonFollowerExchange %}
# Reluctance to let a follower displace this player and non-follower exchange

{% if followerInterruption == 1 %}
Do not select a follower.
{% elif followerInterruption == 2 %}
Give the recipient or `0` a very strong preference over a follower. Select a follower only when their immediate reaction is unusually specific to this moment and omitting it would make their supplied character information difficult to reconcile with the scene.
{% elif followerInterruption == 3 %}
Prefer the recipient or `0`, but allow a follower whose immediate reaction is clearly specific to this exchange and more timely than waiting for the recipient.
{% elif followerInterruption == 4 %}
Give the recipient a modest preference. A follower may speak whenever their supported reaction belongs naturally at this point in the exchange.
{% else %}
Apply no preference against followers. Compare them with the recipient and other permitted candidates using the same selection standard.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if hasExchange %}
# Reluctance to let an unrelated non-follower displace this exchange

{% if nonFollowerInterruption == 1 %}
Do not select a non-follower who is not already part of the exchange.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 2 %}
Give the recipient or `0` a very strong preference over an unrelated non-follower. Select one only when their immediate reaction is unusually specific to this moment and omitting it would make their supplied role or character information difficult to reconcile with the scene.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 3 %}
Prefer the recipient or `0`, but allow an unrelated non-follower whose supported reaction is clearly specific to this exchange and more timely than waiting for the recipient.
{% else %}
Give the recipient only a modest preference. An unrelated non-follower may speak whenever their supported reaction belongs naturally at this point in the exchange.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if playerWasAddressed %}
The player was addressed. `0` is the natural result unless a permitted candidate has an immediate reaction that should occur before the player answers.
{% elif silenceAllowed %}
Choose `0` when the exchange has naturally ended or no permitted candidate has a supported immediate reaction.
{% endif %}

Do not select an NPC to comment on silence, urge the player to respond, or narrate waiting.

# Virtual NPC restrictions

- A regular NPC cannot hear or answer a Virtual NPC.
- A regular NPC cannot target a Virtual NPC.
- A Virtual NPC may target another Virtual NPC.

{{ get_scene_context(0, 0, "full") }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
# Location

{{ location }}

# Recent Dialogue

{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}

{% if hasExchange %}
# Completed line

**{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke to {{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}.**
{% endif %}

# Candidates

{% for candidate in candidateDialogues %}
{% if candidate.UUID and candidate.UUID != 0 %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(candidate.UUID) %}
{{ candidate.id }}. **{{ cinfo.name }}**{% if hasExchange and candidate.UUID == lastDialogueTarget.UUID %} **[RECIPIENT]**{% endif %}{% if hasExchange and candidate.UUID == lastSpeaker.UUID %} **[PREVIOUS SPEAKER — DO NOT SELECT]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) %} **[FOLLOWER]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and tagEngaged and is_in_package(candidate.UUID, "SkyrimNet_PlayerFollowPackage") %} **[ENGAGED]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and tagInScene and (is_in_faction(candidate.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction") or is_in_faction(candidate.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction")) %} **[IN SCENE]**{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %} **[VIRTUAL NPC]**{% endif %}
   - {% if not cinfo.isVirtual %}{{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(candidate.distance) }}m — {% endif %}{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", candidate.UUID) }}
   - **Interjection:** {{ render_character_profile("interject_inline", candidate.UUID) }}
{% if playerNonFollowerExchange and not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) and followerInterruption >= 4 %}
   - **Personality:** {{ render_character_profile("bio_personality", candidate.UUID) }}
{% elif hasExchange and not cinfo.isVirtual and not is_follower(candidate.UUID) and candidate.UUID != lastSpeaker.UUID and candidate.UUID != lastDialogueTarget.UUID and nonFollowerInterruption == 4 %}
   - **Personality:** {{ render_character_profile("bio_personality", candidate.UUID) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

`[ENGAGED]` is supporting context, not permission to override an interruption instruction. Strongly avoid `[IN SCENE]` unless directly addressed.

# Targeting

{% if playerSpoke %}
- A responding `[RECIPIENT]` targets `player`.
{% else %}
- A responding `[RECIPIENT]` targets {{ lastSpeaker.name }}.
{% endif %}
- Another speaker targets the person their reaction addresses.
- Use `player` in lowercase when the player is the target.
- Otherwise use an exact full candidate name.
- Always include a target.

Valid outputs:

- `Aela the Huntress>Lydia`
{% if silenceAllowed %}
- `0`
{% endif %}

Do not add tags, formatting, explanation, or shortened names.

Output:
[ end user ]
